{"code":""""O(n) single-pass maximum-drawdown implementation."""

from __future__ import annotations


def max_drawdown(prices: list[float]) -> float:
    if len(prices) < 2:
        return 0.0

    largest = 0.0
    peak = prices[0]

    for price in prices[1:]:
        if price > peak:
            peak = price
        else:
            drawdown = (peak - price) / peak
            if drawdown > largest:
                largest = drawdown

    return largest","notes":"Replaced O(n²) nested loops with O(n) single pass. Track running peak; compute drawdown only when current price falls below peak. Handles edge cases: empty/one-element returns 0.0, non-decreasing series never updates largest, decreasing series captures full drop from initial peak."}
